dzn: Clear and resolve attachments in their view format

A mutable image used through a view of another format was cleared through
a render target view in the image's format, and the copy fallback packed
the clear colour in the image's format, so the image got the wrong bits.
Render pass resolves built their views and pipeline from the image formats
too, converting the values instead of reinterpreting the bits; they now
take the blit path when a view's format differs from its image's.

From Oliver Bestmann's commits e04f004 and 05ce00a in
github.com/weaselway/mesa (MIT), where dEQP-VK.image.mutable.*load_op_clear*
and *resolve* pass (25 failed before).

